    {
      "id": "hx63nie",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a longitudinal mechanical wave that requires a material medium to propagate and cannot travel through a vacuum.",
        "The pitch of a sound is determined by its frequency, while its loudness is proportional to the square of the amplitude.",
        "An echo requires a minimum distance of 17.2 meters between the sound source and the reflecting surface, along with a time interval of at least 0.1 seconds.",
        "Ultrasound waves have frequencies above 20,000 Hz and are extensively used in medical imaging (SONAR, echocardiography) and industrial flaw detection.",
        "The speed of sound depends on the medium's density and elasticity, traveling fastest in solids, slower in liquids, and slowest in gases."
      ],
      "id": "uuarzsq"
    },
