    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Speed of Sound order: Solids > Liquids > Gases. Sound speed is ZERO in a vacuum.",
        "Loudness is proportional to the square of the amplitude (if amplitude doubles, loudness increases by 4x).",
        "SONAR utilizes ultrasonic waves to measure underwater depth and locate submerged objects based on sound reflection.",
        "The persistence of hearing for the human ear is 0.1 seconds, which dictates the minimum distance required for hearing a clear echo."
      ],
